// Decline golden: the retired constructor-block spelling (ADR-52 Decision C:
// pathological tree, testing artifact).
//
// The Haskell/OCaml-style data declaration — bare head parameters, no head
// annotation, field-tuple members — is RETIRED: the one form is the nested
// generator block, whose head binds every parameter as a typed binder and
// carries the index-arity annotation. The grammar keeps the old spelling
// admissible so the stage-0 elaborator can decline it with the respelling
// (the retired-`~>` precedent) rather than the parser repairing a token. The
// head declines first — bare `a` carries no type — and the whole declaration
// is skipped; with a valid head the retired members would decline
// individually, each told its generator-judgment respelling.
data Maybe(a) { None, Some(x: a) }

//@ mode: desc
//@ expect-desc-decline: carries no type
